  "kanji": "冊",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 冊\ntitle: volume; book counter\njlpt: 2\ntags: [jlpt-n2, grade-6, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 5\nradical: 冂\nradicalNumber: 13\nonyomi: [サツ, サク]\nkunyomi: [ふみ]\ndistractors: [曲, 用, 西]\n---\n\n# 冊 — volume; book counter\n\n**Strokes:** 5 · **Key (radical):** 冂 (no. 13) · **JLPT:** N2 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n冊 is used to count books and bound volumes. 冊子 さっし means a book, booklet, or pamphlet. The counter and the lexical word have related meanings, but their pronunciations must be learned with their whole forms.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** Imagine the upright strokes as several pages joined together by the long horizontal stroke.\n\nThe classical indexing radical is 冂, the outer enclosure-like shape; it is not a separate word within 冊.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| サツ | on | 冊 さつ - counter for books |\n| サク | on | 冊封 さくほう - bestowing peerage by imperial edict in ancient China (historical term) |\n| ふみ | kun | Source-only reading; see the qualification below. |\n\nKANJIDIC2 also records `ふみ`. No matching word example was established in the inspected JMdict snapshot. These are character-dictionary readings for lookup, not recommendations to use this kanji as an everyday spelling of a word.\n\n## Common words\n\n- [冊子](../words/冊子.md) さっし - booklet; pamphlet\n- 冊 さつ - counter for books and bound volumes\n\n## Notes\n\n- 冊子 is さっし, with a small っ. That pronunciation illustrates the サツ series in a compound; it is not evidence for reading this word さくし.\n- The サク example 冊封 is a historical term, not a general everyday word for a booklet. The source-only ふみ reading is not a recommendation to rewrite [文](文.md) or [本](../words/本.md) indiscriminately.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-21 snapshot. Word pairs: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1298520, 1298530, 2786450.\n",
